=2 Walkthrough
* Must zone after previous quest in order to start this quest.
* Speak with {n:Iruki-Waraki} in {p:Aht Urhgan Whitegate} for a cut-scene. You'll discover that he is trying to get his Automaton back, and has formed a plan.
* He gives you a shopping list of items needed to help his plan come to fruition.
* You can be on any job from here on.
** Obtain the required items: {@i:Sleeping Potion|4161} {i:Sleeping Potion|Sleeping Potion|4161} x1, {@i:Chai|5570} {i:Chai|Chai|5570} x1
* Return to {n:Iruki-Waraki} and trade him the items for a cut-scene. He then asks you to arrange a meeting with the thief in {z:Nashmau}.
* Head to {z:Nashmau}, and seek out {n:Dnegan} for a cut-scene(@H-6 on the second floor).
* **Warning:** Do **__NOT**__ select the option "Ask about the Automaton" in this cut-scene. Speaking with him will start a cutscene, during which you will be approached by Yafahb.
** You will be given 3 chat options: Ask about the Automaton, Ask about getting around {z:Nashmau}, or invite the thief to have tea with you. Do **not** ask about the {p:Automaton}!
** If you do, you will end the cutscene and be forced to wait a game day before resuming. Choose either of the other options.
* The next part of the cutscene takes you to {z:Nashmau} Port, and you'll see {n:Iruki|Iruki-Waraki}'s plan in action. He has set-up a tea shop, and as you approach he asks what you would like to drink.
* You are then presented with 3 options. {i:Chai|Chai|5570}, Coffee or "I'll pass, thanks".
** Choose either drink. Regardless of your drink choice, {n:Iruki|Iruki-Waraki} will convince the thief to have {@i:Chai|5570} {i:Chai|Chai|5570}.
*** He will, however, mix up the drinks, leaving you to guess which has the {@i:Sleeping Potion|4161} {i:Sleeping Potion|Sleeping Potion|4161} inside, and which doesn't.
**** **The cup with the "Suspicious Vapour" is the correct choice.**
***** If you make the wrong choice you must wait until the next game day to try again.
****** You do not need to trade the {@i:Chai|5570} {i:Chai|Chai|5570} and {@i:Sleeping Potion|4161} {i:Sleeping Potion|Sleeping Potion|4161} again.
***** The thief then falls asleep. {n:Iruki|Iruki-Waraki} then confronts the Automaton, which runs off into the depths of {z:Caedarva Mire}.
* The next part of this quest is long winded and leaves you stuck in a remote area, so bring either a {@i:Warp Ring|28540} {i:Warp Ring|Warp Ring|28540} or an {@i:Instant Warp|4181} {i:Scroll of Instant Warp|Instant Warp|4181}.
* The final **???** for this quest is located in {z:Caedarva Mire}, at (K-5), which is actually part of the Azouph Isle map. However, you will need to travel through {z:Arrapago Reef} to reach it.
* The quickest way to {z:reef|Arrapago Reef} is the Survival Guide to {z:reef|Arrapago Reef}.
* If you used the survival guide to {z:reef|Arrapago Reef}, zone out then grab yourself a {@i:Lamian Fang Key|2219} {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} and zone into the reef from (I-6). The key can be acquired from a **???** near a pond a short way from the zone.
** If you did not use the Survival guide, take the Azouph Isle staging point then head to I-6 for the {@i:Lamian Fang Key|2219} {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} and then enter {z:reef|Arrapago Reef} entrance 1.
*** Beware of the green "Swamp" water near the {@i:Lamian Fang Key|2219} {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} as it can spawn a NM or debuff you with weight.
*** The Jnun near the {@i:Lamian Fang Key|2219} {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} sleeps during the day and will not aggro.
*** You can also lockpick the door as a thief with thief tools or farm the key from lamia and draugar's inside {z:reef|Arrapago Reef}.
* For the {z:reef|Arrapago Reef} you are going to need {i:Silent Oils|Silent Oil|4165} and {i:Prism Powders|Prism Powder|4164}, sub {p:Dancer}, or etc.
* You'll find yourself at (I-11) on the map when you first zone into {z:reef|Arrapago Reef}.
* Apply {p:Sneak (Status)} and {p:Invisible (Status)}, and run around to the Iron Gate at (J-10). Trade the {@i:Lamian Fang Key|2219} {i:Lamian Fang Key|Lamian Fang Key|2219} to open it, and head inside.
** From inside, take the north path on this map, and you'll reach (J-8) back on the first map. Open the door located there and go through.
** Head to J-6 (Caedarva Mire 6)
*** There is a tunnel entrance at (I-6), not far north from where you are. Head there.
*** Travel East through that tunnel, until presented with a fork in the road. Take the southern route. And run that way until you zone out into {z:Caedarva Mire}.
* Once in Caedarva Mire Apply {p:Invisible (Status)} then head to K-6 and click the ??? behind the tree.
** This area has {m:Mosshorn} rams and {m:Elder Treants|Elder Treant}, so take care not to gain unwanted attention. The **???** you seek is located next to a tree a short distance from the zone.
* Enjoy the final cut-scene. Once it is complete you will receive your {@i:Pup. Churidars|15602} {i:Puppetry Churidars|Puppetry Churidars|15602}.

